#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1053 expect=noViolation domain=TA
#note "Case boundary of the membership test. The Check compiles to the PLAIN case-SENSITIVE is_contained_by, so neither mixed-case spelling matches the uppercase CT submission values and the rule is silent -- correct, since a lower-case ARMCD is a different (CT) conformance failure this rule does not own. ARMCD is present, so the injected var_exists guard holds and the rule EXECUTES (not skipped)."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset TA label="Trial Arms"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col ARMCD   type=Char label="Planned Arm Code"
col ARM     type=Char label="Description of Planned Arm"
col TAETORD type=Num  label="Planned Order of Element within Arm"
---
S1 | TA | Scrnfail | Screen Failure | 1
S1 | TA | notassgn | Not Assigned   | 1
S1 | TA | A        | Drug X 10 mg   | 1
